*.log
.DS_Store
# Every .env variant, not a list of the ones somebody thought of.
#
# This was exactly `.env`, `.env.backup`, `.env.production`, and a real file
# slipped between them: `api/.env.bak.1785852708`, written by a script that
# timestamps its backup. It matched none of the three and sat untracked in the
# demo worktree, one `git add -A` away from being published — and this
# repository is public. A .env carries APP_KEY and the database credentials.
#
# The glob is deliberately wide. A secret leaking because the pattern was too
# narrow costs far more than a config sample needing `git add -f`.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
.phpactor.json
.phpunit.result.cache
/.codex
/.cursor/
/.idea
/.nova
/.phpunit.cache
/.vscode
/.zed
/auth.json
/node_modules
/public/build
/public/fonts-manifest.dev.json
/public/hot
/public/storage
/storage/*.key
/storage/pail
/vendor
_ide_helper.php
Homestead.json
Homestead.yaml
Thumbs.db
/database/database.sqlite
/storage/app/backups
